Task 8: Safe Input Validation
1. cin.fail()
It checks whether an input operation has failed, such as when the user enters letters instead of a number.
2. cin.clear()
It clears the error state of the input stream so that input can continue.
3. cin.ignore()
It removes unwanted characters from the input buffer.
4. iomanip
The `iomanip` header provides formatting tools such as `fixed` and `setprecision()` to display money with two decimal places.
Conclusion
Input validation prevents invalid values from being processed and improves the reliability of the Metro Smart-Card System.
